{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "עגלות", :translit "agalot", :gloss "wagons"} {:he "עגלה ערופה", :translit "eglah arufah", :gloss "broken-necked heifer"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["עגלות"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["עגלה ערופה"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase עגלה ערופה appears four times in the section of Deuteronomy 21:1–9 dealing with the ritual of the broken-necked heifer, where the elders of the city nearest an undiscovered corpse decapitate a heifer in a wadi and declare 'Our hands did not shed this blood' (Deuteronomy 21:7). Jacob's seeing the wagons (עגלות) that Joseph sent (Genesis 45:27) revives his spirit because they signal that Joseph remembered the last topic they had studied together before separating.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 21:1–9" "Genesis 45:27" "Bereshit Rabbah 100:3" "Tanchuma Vayigash 12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וירא את העגלות", :translit "vayar et ha-agalot", :gloss "and he saw the wagons"} {:he "ראה בהלכת עגלה ערופה", :translit "re'eh behilkhat eglah arufah", :gloss "see [in] the laws of the broken-necked heifer"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וירא את העגלות", :b "ראה בהלכת עגלה ערופה"}], :frame {:text "Joseph sent wagons (עגלות, Genesis 45:27) as a coded message to Jacob, recalling the last Torah subject they had studied together before Joseph was sold — the laws of עגלה ערופה (Deuteronomy 21:1–9). The shared sound root עגל links עגלות (wagons) with עגלה (heifer), and the gematria equating וירא את העגלות with ראה בהלכת עגלה ערופה compresses the teaching that Jacob 'saw' in the wagons a reference back to that study.", :sources ["Genesis 45:27" "Deuteronomy 21:1–9" "Bereshit Rabbah 100:3" "Tanchuma Vayigash 12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["עגלות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "עגלות", :refs ["Genesis 45:19" "Genesis 45:21" "1 Kings 7:31" "Psalms 46:10"], :n 4, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["עגלה ערופה"], :by :selah,